# Docker Compose ships a safe loopback-only default for both of these (see compose.yaml),
# so `docker compose up` works from a fresh checkout with no .env file at all. Override them
# here for anything beyond a single trusted operator on localhost.
# Generate a value: python -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))'
HARVEST_API_TOKEN=replace-this-with-a-random-token-before-starting
HARVEST_USER_AGENT=HarvestPlatform/0.5
# HARVEST_CA_BUNDLE=/path/to/trusted-ca.pem
# Optional: your SearXNG instance, with JSON enabled in search.formats.
# HARVEST_SEARCH_URL=http://searxng:8080
# HARVEST_PRIVATE_HOSTS=searxng
# Optional: external OSINT CLIs allowed to run as acquisition tasks, comma separated.
# Empty (the default) means none may run. Each named tool must be installed in the worker
# image. These make their own requests outside the fetcher's budget and rate limits, so
# enable only what the engagement authorizes.
# HARVEST_TOOLS=maigret
# HARVEST_TOOL_TIMEOUT=600
# Retry transient failures for individual Maigret sites (0-3, default 0). This can
# increase its unbudgeted outbound requests; the full tool task is never retried.
# HARVEST_MAIGRET_RETRIES=1
# Requires a separately running, configured Cloudflare bypass service reachable
# from the Maigret worker. It is not an egress proxy or a privacy control.
# HARVEST_MAIGRET_CLOUDFLARE_BYPASS=true
# Optional: SpiderFoot NG REST API, reached over a private network only. The key is a
# bearer credential sent on every call, so do not point this at a public address.
# Enable the tool with HARVEST_TOOLS=spiderfoot as well.
# HARVEST_SPIDERFOOT_URL=http://sf-api:8001
# HARVEST_SPIDERFOOT_API_KEY=
# Modules a scan may run. The default is one passive resolver; SpiderFoot's full set is
# active reconnaissance against the target, which is an authorization decision.
# HARVEST_SPIDERFOOT_MODULES=sfp_dnsresolve
# Optional: a Chat Completions-compatible endpoint (including local models).
# HARVEST_MODEL_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# HARVEST_MODEL_NAME=your-model
# HARVEST_MODEL_KEY=
# Upper-bound USD per million input/output tokens. Use 0 for a local model.
# HARVEST_MODEL_USD_PER_MILLION=0
# Optional trusted egress proxy with remote DNS. The fetcher only proxies listed
# public hosts; Maigret uses its own site list when --proxy is enabled.
# Supported schemes: http, https, socks5, socks5h -- credentials may be embedded,
# e.g. http://user:pass@proxy.example.net:8080 for an HTTP ISP proxy.
# HARVEST_EGRESS_PROXY=socks5://your-proxy:1080
# When enabled, Maigret's main checks use this proxy. Its automatic site-database update
# is disabled, but auxiliary activation requests still need network-level egress controls.
# HARVEST_PROXY_PUBLIC_HOSTS=www.python.org,api.github.com
#
# Egress mode. "direct" (default) is the historical behaviour. "proxy" is fail-closed:
# it requires HARVEST_EGRESS_PROXY, refuses the Cloudflare bypass (FlareSolverr egresses
# from its own container), refuses a SpiderFoot scan unless SpiderFoot's own global proxy
# matches this one, and refuses to run Maigret at all unless direct egress is actually
# blocked at the network level -- because Maigret's activation helpers ignore --proxy.
# HARVEST_EGRESS_MODE=proxy
# The address proxy mode probes to confirm direct egress is blocked. It must NOT be
# reachable without the proxy; if the probe connects, tools refuse to run.
# HARVEST_EGRESS_PROBE=1.1.1.1:443

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COMPOSE_FILE -- read by every bare `docker compose` command in this directory.
#
# Set this on any deployment that relies on overlay files. Without it, the overlays
# are only applied when an operator remembers to name them with -f, and the commands
# that skip them still report success: `up -d` prints "Started" with the stack in
# direct egress mode and the API published on 0.0.0.0, and `build` prints "Built" for
# an image containing none of the external tools. Naming them here removes the choice.
#
# An explicit -f on the command line replaces this value entirely, so do not pass one.
# `docker compose down -v` will remove the volumes of every listed overlay.
#
# COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.override.yaml:compose.egress-proxy.yaml:compose.ghunt.yaml
